---
title: "Global attributes"
description: "The data-ui-* attributes no primitive owns."
section: Foundations
sectionOrder: 1
order: 5
---

Everything a primitive owns is `data-<primitive>-*`. Four attributes belong to the page instead and keep the `data-ui-` prefix.

{% globals /%}

## Theme

`data-ui-theme="dark"` or `"light"` on any element pins that scheme for the subtree; it only sets `color-scheme`, so scopes nest and every `light-dark()` token follows. Without it, the page follows the system. The head's theme script sets the attribute on `<html>` from `localStorage.theme` before first paint.

## Navigation and persistence

With `data-ui-navigation="swap"` on `<html>`, a same-origin navigation between two opted-in pages fetches the destination and swaps the whole `<body>` in place. Nothing survives the swap unless it carries `data-ui-persist="<id>"` on both pages; then the live element moves into the new page with its state and scroll offsets, and its links take `aria-current` from the new page. `data-ui-persist-scroll="<id>"` renders an element from the new page but keeps its scroll offset, for a region whose content changes per page, such as a sidebar. Reloads, hash changes, downloads, and form posts are never intercepted. See [navigation](/api/javascript/navigation/).

## Style guard

`data-ui-guard="off"` opts an element out of the [style guard](/api/primitives/style-guard/), which otherwise restores style utilities a legacy script overwrites.
